 "title": "Cold Pitching Founder Content Strategy to B2B Perfume Distributor",
 "topic": "sales",
 "summary": "A content strategist approaches a B2B perfume distributor in person to pitch founder-focused content services. When the founder objects that B2B companies do not need consumer-style content, she explains how personal brand trust drives B2B decisions and successfully secures a meeting.",
 "key_points": [
  "Ask directly to speak with the company founder or primary decision-maker when cold pitching in person.",
  "Overcome the B2B objection by explaining that B2B marketing relies heavily on trust, personal branding, and platforms like LinkedIn.",
  "Position content around building credibility and trust rather than vanity metrics like views and followers.",
  "Offer flexible arrangements, such as traveling to the founder's location to shoot content, to remove logistical hurdles.",
  "Close the pitch by asking directly for their phone number to schedule a follow-up conversation."
 ],
 "content": "Post Text:\nNot one of those people who think just cause u have a company u deserve customers \n\nFounders I’m going to find you all\n\nMake a note of this post.\n\nTranscript:\nSwara: Hi, is this your Instagram account for the company?\nDistributor Staff: Yes.\nSwara: So I just wanna let you know I'm a founder of brand uh content strategist, and I create content especially for founders. And have you guys tried something like that before?\nDistributor Staff: It's a B2B company. We are not B2C.\nSwara: Okay. So what I understand is B2B focuses more on LinkedIn, and even on in any form of marketing, trust with the founder is most important. So if I could get a 15-minute talk with your founder... Is your founder here? Can I... Hi! So this company is after your name. How are you?\nAbhinav: Good, how are you?\nSwara: What are your thoughts on creating content for your own page?\nAbhinav: Too tired right now to talk now.\nSwara: No, that's okay. Here's what's happening in Dubai in the perfume industry, right? All the big brands that are out here, they are banking on the branding, right? But the brands that are up and coming, which have your name associated with it, people wanna know who Abhinav is, right? So essentially, doing content for your company...\nAbhinav: I think makes no sense. We are a B2B company.\nSwara: Uh-huh, yeah. How do you guys usually reach customers? I know you guys work with businesses, but what essentially happens is even in B2B, there are so many options for people to pick. Trust is what I'm marketing. I'm not marketing the fact that you're going to get views, follows.\nAbhinav: Do you work remotely as well?\nSwara: I mean, if you hire me, I can fly to India and shoot content and do it. Look, I'm all about great founder brands.\nAbhinav: I wish, I wish I can do that.\nSwara: Why wish? Of course you can. I'm gonna get your number, yeah?\nAbhinav: Yeah.\n\nOn-screen text:\n- Cold pitching Founder content to a B2B perfume distributor (Booked a meeting yayle)\n- *doesn't matter we are a B2B company",
